  "what_changed": "Pit-race screen for the paired Core2, on top of 2026-11-13-upstream-036. The Heltec display line gains race_hold, race_go_ms and race_went_ms; the Core2 shows GRID HOLD with a countdown, GO for three seconds after the Heltec reports releasing the kart, and RACE / FINISHED with the position from the pit beacon. Display only: the only change outside reporting is one timestamp recorded when a grid hold ends in a GO on a kart that is not stopped. All three Heltec kart images and all three Core2 images are rebuilt; base and repeater are unchanged.",
  "compatibility": "Both boards of a kart should be updated together to get the countdown: an older Heltec does not send the new fields and an older Core2 ignores them, and either mix otherwise behaves as before. The LoRa protocol and the course package (rules version 2) are unchanged. Host Heltec, host Pi server, player Heltec and player Core2 must all be from this source for course download, JOIN and FIRE. An M5 kart cannot join a ROAM freeplay.",
